<title>BELGIUM: Dutch BNG bought less than 3 pct Dexia in market.</title>
<headline>Dutch BNG bought less than 3 pct Dexia in market.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB), the Belgian arm of Belgian-French alliance Dexia, said on Monday Dutch Bank der Nederlandsche Gemeenten (BNG) bought a small stake in Dexia.</p>
<p>&quot;BNG has been buying shares in Dexia on the Brussels bourse. We do not know how much, but we assume it was less than three percent of our capital. Otherwise it would been notified officially,&quot; CCB chief executive officer Francois Narmon told a news conference.</p>
<p>BNG already has a five percent stake in Credit Local de France (CLF), the French arm of Dexia.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
